"""Every current-affairs question of the 2018, 2021 and 2025 GA papers, dated against its own exam.
Used by tools/build_ca_pyq_analysis.py (writes ASO-CA-PYQ-Analysis-2027.html).

One tuple per question: (q, fam, ym, when, ask, answer, note, check)
  fam   family code (FAMS below)
  ym    "YYYY-MM" month of the news; "fixed" for a date that never changes;
        "run" for a running story with no single date; None when the date was not traced
  when  how the date reads on the page
  note  what the question shows, in plain words; markup: **bold**, ⟦2025 Q10⟧, ⟨CHECK⟩
Keys are ours (no official key exists), checked against the Udyam IAS books and the news.
Exam dates: 2018 paper on 20 Jan 2019 (moved from 23 Dec 2018); 2021 paper on 27 Aug 2022
(moved from 21 Aug for floods); 2025 paper on 9 Nov 2025.
"""

FAMS = [
    ("DEF", "Defence, security and operations"),
    ("DAY", "Days, themes and dates"),
    ("ORG", "Summits and world bodies"),
    ("GOV", "Schemes, ministries and national firsts"),
    ("WLD", "World news, leaders and world firsts"),
    ("ODI", "Odisha"),
    ("ENV", "Environment and forests"),
    ("SCI", "Space and science"),
    ("CRT", "Courts and the Constitution"),
    ("GEO", "Geography in the news"),
    ("RPT", "Reports and ranks"),
    ("ECO", "Budget, RBI and the economy"),
    ("AWD", "Awards, books, sports and personalities"),
]

